@using Microsoft.FeatureManagement
@using static SAPPub.Web.Constants.Constants;
@inject Microsoft.FeatureManagement.IFeatureManager FeatureManager

<h4 class="govuk-heading-m">Low, medium and high prior attainers</h4>
<p class="govuk-body">
    At the end of key stage 1 (year 2), most pupils are assessed in English reading, English writing and maths.
</p>
<p class="govuk-body">
    Pupils are given a combined average point score across reading, writing and maths between 0 and 10 and are then allocated a group:
</p>
<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>low prior attainers achieved an average point score of below 7</li>
    <li>middle prior attainers achieved a point score of 7 or higher but less than or equal to 8</li>
    <li>high prior attainers achieved an average score higher than 8</li>
</ul>
@if (await FeatureManager.IsEnabledAsync(EnableKS2PupilCharacteristicDropdown))
{
    <text>
        Pupils are groups into low, middle and high prior attainers based on their results at the end of KS1.
        These figures show how each group performance at the end of KS2, helping you understand how well the school supports pupils with diffrent starting points. Pupils without KS1 results are not included.
    </text>
}
else
{
    <text>
        There is no KS2 measures by prior attainment for academic years 2023 to 2024 and 2024 to 2025.
        This is because there is no KS1 prior attainment data available for these pupils due to COVID - 19 disruption.
    </text>
}
